{
  "_comment": "Shared end-to-end search match/filter vectors: raw query strings plus recipe documents in, matched recipe ids in final display order out. Consumed by tests/test_search_match_filter_vectors.py (which replays the corpus through the real API and database, timestamps included) and by SearchMatchFilterSharedVectorTests on iOS (which replays it through the Swift local-search pipeline). ingredient_match_text is the stored ingredients JSON exactly as the server writes it (compact, keys sorted) — copied from the database, never hand-written — and is the exact haystack bare-text tokens match against. Expected orders never depend on recipe-id tie-breaks (server ids are random UUIDs); score ties are resolved by distinct updated_at values instead. sort_by/sort_dir omitted means server defaults (relevance with text terms, updated_at desc without). source_name is what source: matches; kcal_per_serving is what calories: filters and the calories sort compare (the harness writes it to the database, since the server derives it); photo holds the stored file size and pixel dimensions photo_size: and photo_dim: compare, null for a recipe without a photo, with null facts for a photo whose facts are unknown.",
